\f0\fs24 \cf2 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 Halo sipped beer in a bar and reflected on how well his vacation was progressing. All the broadcast screens around him beamed the formal swearing in and commissioning by the Governor Capitalist General of the new Commissioner of TRAMPS, one Gerald Hardman, a deep PAPER plant in the force. Halo was so pleased with himself, he felt no urgent appetite for killing, lawn bowls or knitting. He even caught himself being kinder and more respectful to bar waitresses and female customers alike. His newfound loss of misogyny terrified them almost as much as the dulling of his creepy eyes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Images of Very Hardman raising his hand appeared across a battery of screens. As he recited the Oath of Property Protection and Allegiance to the Status Quo, Halo contemplated the final day trip of his vacation: busting Chanta out of Truth Central\'97a PAPER installation to which Halo had or could acquire all skeleton keys and security passes.\
Imagine the temperature of his supernova-grade fury when he later discovered the Elvi had beaten him to it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 It was another average morning for Chanta: wake-up call at six; cold shower at half-past; breakfast gruel at seven, accompanied by a mug of tea that smelled and tasted as if fish had been dying in it; make-up at seven-thirty; green room at eight-thirty; interrogation and torture at nine sharp.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 All the usual tormentors were there: Special Agent Ajent Jones wearing a black suit with a glistening green tie, and a cast of henches in ceremonial, identity-hiding hoods, plus a full production team and camera crew from 
\f2\i C.Y.I.
\f1\i0  Of all present, Chanta hated most the one who seemed entirely unaffected by his psychological and physical suffering.\
It was still another average morning at 9:04 a.m. At 9:05, recording was halted by the sounds of explosions. The walls of Truth Central shook. The far end of the studio crumbled; over the rubble lumbered a tank, gun barrel aimed at the director\'92s chair.\
As furious as Special Agent Jones was, even he joined his colleagues in fleeing the scene, as did all the 
\f2\i C.Y.I.
\f1\i0  team\'97except for one camera operator, who kept framing and recording.\
The turret hatch of the tank clanged open and an Elvis emerged, resplendent in a camouflage jumpsuit and matching cape. \'93Good morning, Mr Tony, sir. I\'92m Specialist Five Tulsa McLean. In the name of the Holy Momma, we\'92ve come to rescue you.\'94
